  "_comment": "What GivTCP does per inverter model, and where HEM or the simulator knowingly differs. GivTCP has far more users testing it on real hardware, so it is the reference for model capability. Checked offline by src-tauri/src/inverter/givtcp_contract.rs, tests/lib/givtcpContract.test.ts, e2e/local-model-contract.spec.ts (every simulator model through the backend) and the simulator's crates/sim-registers/tests/givtcp_contract.rs, which reads an identical copy (tests/scripts/check-givtcp-contract.test.py, in npm test, compares the two when the simulator is checked out next to HEM). npm run check:givtcp (scripts/check-givtcp-contract.py) re-reads GivTCP itself before a release. pause: none, mode (HR 318 only) or mode_and_window (HR 318-320). three_phase: the HR 1000+ schedule and control bank. charge_cap: HEM's charge cap (issue #426) is offered, which GivTCP's pause implies. A deviation is a known difference: its value is what HEM (or the simulator) does instead, with the issue that will remove it, or why it stays.",
